I DID IT! I FINALLY DID IT!
Tonight at 03:57 AM, Grawl the mighty orcish barbarian finally ascended
to demigod-hood as the first of hundreds of characters who had died at
my hands during the past few years.

The first time I "played" NH was at the age of 9 (or 10, can't
remember) on my daddy's Atari 1024 ST. Of course, I didn't quite know
what I was doing, hell I didn't even know English back then :-)
Then I re-discovered the game when I got my first PC and internet
access in 1996 (at the age of 13). Since then, I had been playing every
now and then, but I rarely managed to get past the castle. I took a
long break when a very promising valkyrie died to an endless horde of
horned devils on the plane of air (god knows where they all came from).
She died six times and finally ran out of =oLS. Totally frustrated, I
wouldn't touch the game for a long time.

Then, about two weeks ago, I started playing barbarians. And now I can
finally tell everyone I beat Nethack :-)


Now let's see if I can remember some details...

- Started out with *very* good stats: 18/02 STR, 18 DEX, 18 CON without
stats-scumming or whatever you call it.
- Annoying dungeon layout. Only 2 shops (tiny bookstore on L3, quality
apparel shop on L3 with a large assortment of crap wands), almost no
special rooms or vaults, first altar on L11.
- Had to wait with the mines until I got some light source as they were
*all* dark levels except minetown.
- Got =oR from Sokoban, would have preferred the bag as I was lugging
around tons of stuff (remember, no altar).
- Finally had to hack my way through the dark mines with a thorougly
rusty and corroded battle axe and AC:8 when a polymorphed mumak blocked
my way on L10.
- Minetown was lit, woohoo! The general store only had useless stuff
(no magic lamp *sigh*), the bookstore only had spellbooks (no ?oID
*sigh*), the deli at least had 2 tins of spinach. Izchak had enough
candles for 4 or 5 invocations, but no magic lamp either (*sigh*). And
the temple was cross-aligned *double sigh*. I became frustrated and
thought of committing suicide by throwing cream pies (from the local
deli) at the priest of Crom.
- Nevertheless I returned to the dungeons and continued. Found
cross-aligned temples (argh) on L11 and L14, but L14 had a second
altar, cross-aligned but unoccupied. I converted it and set up my first
base camp there.
- After lugging down all the crap I had collected, I went down to L15
only to find a co-aligned altar in the first room there. duh!

- A sacrificing session produced Cleaver and a wraith corpse, which
allowed me to do the quest. The 3rd quest level had the bones of
Gruumsh, my most promising barbarian so far, who had been paralyzed and
killed by a horde of ogres and rock trolls. I gladly looted a CoMR, a
pair of GoP (rusty and corroded, but who cares), fireproof speed boots,
a tinning kit, a (still blessed) bag of holding and my first reliable
light source in form of a magic lamp - hurray! Kicked Thoth Amon's arse
with ease and went back to my dungeon camp.
- Prepared and sacced some more, but even hundreds of corpses yielded
no other artifacts. Genocided "h", did the rest of the mines, then
noticed I could have skipped them since the Heart of Ahriman wasn't a
flint stone but a luckstone.
- Went down to face Medusa. The titan decided to be a jerk and summoned
a minotaur and two or three other heavy hitters when I came down the
stairs. They brought me from 124 HP to 34 HP in one move, so I hauled
my orcish ass back up and decided to call it a tactical retreat if
anyone asked.
- Found the portal to Fort Ludios on L19 and looted the place clean.
The silver dragon scales I found merged into a nice 'n shiny new armor.
Bought some more protection with all the money and did some alchemy to
beef up HP.
- Sacrificed ~50 more corpses (emptying 13 wands and 2 bags of tricks)
without getting anything, but found another magic lamp on one of the
monsters I had created. Wished for a magic marker and enchanted some of
my armor. When I finally decided to face the titan, I had to kill a
leprechaun on the stairs. I dragged the corpse back to the altar for
one last sacrifice. "Use my gift wisely!". See, that wasn't so hard,
was it? My god had coughed up Frostbrand as a second artifact gift.
Yeah!
- On the level above Medusa, I put on my water walking boots, blinded
myself and zapped a /oDigging down, hoping to land somewhere outside
the room so I could face the titan on my terms. I landed right next to
him *duh* and decided to pull another tactical retreat by zapping the
wand again. Jumped down into some maze.
- Went back up to Medusa, killed her and found the titan alone in his
little room. All the other monsters had jumped down into the maze
through my hole. Idiots.

- Proceeded to the castle, opened the drawbridge and cleared out most
of the bad guys. Before looting anything, I decided to make a quick
trip to my stash as I was burdened already. In one of the maze levels,
I was digging a corridor between the stairs when suddenly a master lich
showed up. Oh crap! "You feel a malignant aura surrounding you". I
wanted to change back to Frostbrand to kill it. But wait... - yeah, you
guessed it. The bastard had cursed the pickaxe. I learned that a
thorougly rusty and corroded pickaxe is *not* the weapon of choice to
combat master liches, so I pulled yet-another-tactical-retreat (YATR
[tm]) through the floor.
- Back at the castle, I noticed I had no means of removing the curse.
No scrolls, no holy water, no nothing. Desperately, I asked Set for
help. "You feel that Set is displeased." SAY WHAT?! It's been some
thousand turns since I last prayed! So, there I was, stuck at the
castle, having just lost my divine protection, with a pissed off deity,
a master lich waiting upstairs and a pickaxe welded to my hand.
- I couldn't think of any rational solution to my dilemma, and feeling
somewhat adventurous, I decided to make a run for it. At least, I had
magic resistance. So I went upstairs, teleported myself away. Three
turns later, the master lich apparently had copied my idea and ended up
right next to me. I pickaxed through some baddies and, to my surprise,
made it to the stairs alive. I escaped.
- A long sacfest followed. After a long time, I managed to hack a
baluchiterium to death on the altar, which finally mollified Set. A
desperate prayer then removed the freakin' pickaxe from my hands and
uncursed all the items the lich had cursed.

- Ok, time to get that protection back. Camped at the altar some more
*yawn* until a cockatrice showed up and left a corpse. I took it and
went upstairs to give the priestess of Mitra a stoning experience.
Reclaimed my 114,000$, gave it to the minetown dude (had to go there to
get some candles anyway) and brought my naked AC back down to -1.
- Used the castle wand to wish for a /oPoly, which I hadn't seen so
far. It came with 4 charges, so I had to polypile efficiently. Got
nothing terribly useful besides a magic marker (78 charges) and two
scrolls of genocide, which I used to wipe out "L" and "R" (I just hate
disenchanters).

- I camped for a long time, sacrificing and praying a lot, got crowned
and slowly spiced up my AC. Enchanted both Frostbrand and a silver
saber (thanks again for the advice, guys :-) to +7, wished for a helm
of ESP (got tired of the rusty dwarven helm I had been wearing all the
time), did some alchemy to boost my HP and finally left the camp to
turn hell upside down. I felt quite invincible by now.
- Fully mapped all of Gehennom without any problems, hoping to find
some nice loot. Got another magic lamp on L47, but never used it. Two
randomly generated Archons came with Sunsword and Demonbane, which I
promptly grabbed for my collection of artifacts. Finally, I found the
vibrating square on L48.
- Went back up and prepared for the run. I put all valuable souvenirs
in a BoH and placed it next to the upstairs on L1, ready to grab it
before leaving the dungeon. Genocided ";" (because everyone does it!),
assembled my survival kit consisting of various =oLS, rings of
conflict/levitation/slow digestion/free action, some magical armor,
scrolls, potions, food, holy water, tons of wands and other useful
things. Then I grabbed the invocation artifacts and left to face the
wizard.

- Killed the wizard in meelee to preserve /oD charges (easy enough),
grabbed the book and did the invocation. Got surrounded by lots of
undead stuff because I forgot to light the candelabrum. duh! Fought my
way through the sanctum, whacked the high priest, grabbed the amulet
and escaped the place via c!oGL.
- The force was nice and only teleported me within the current level
most of the time, only kicked me back to the previous level twice.
Rodney showed up three times, but didn't cause any problems. Well, at
least that's what I thought. You'll see what I mean later.
- Did one a last pit stop at my altar camp on L15, said goodbye to my
peaceful pet brown mold who had been sitting next to the altar all the
time, went up to L1, grabbed my blessed greased bag of assorted trash
(TM) and left for the planes.

- Earth was easy enough. There was a titan on the level, but he never
reached me, nor did the monsters he summoned. Killed some elementals
and xorns, dug my way to the portal using a wand, got rid of the heavy
pickaxe to become unburdened.
- The Plane of Air! This was as far as I had gotten previously. Well,
time to levitate! Now where'd I put that Heart of... #invoke, "i". You
don't have that object. Huh? ... argh! That wizard bastard had stolen
the Heart of Ahriman and I hadn't even noticed! Luckily, I had prepared
for everything and brought a ring of levitation. Phew. Proceeded to
whack some vortices and air elementals. Boy, those things hurt! They
brought me down from ~700 HP to 500 once! *gasp* .. uhm, yeah. I got to
the portal without any problems.
- On Fire, I put on my ring of conflict. I decided not to kill anything
because I had to scroll through gazillions of annoying messages of some
fire monster hitting a fire trap and being unhurt after every move.
God, I have to get out of here.
- Spent some time on Water killing elementals when I finally detected
the portal only three squares away! I took the chance and made a run
for it without further thinking.

- A mysterious voice boomed out "If you want conflict, you shall get
it!" or something along those lines. Uh, crap. Should have taken off
that ring before taking the portal. Whatever, I'm a mighty barbarian
and who needs guardian angels anyway. Whacked all of them and went for
the door.
- Pestilence was waiting right behind it, together with some priests.
You want some death ray? Fine.
- I went straight for the middle and reached it easily. Before I got to
the temple door, Pestilence showed up again and made me ill. *plop*,
nothing a good old unihorn can't cure. I felt cocky and hit him in
meelee. *plop* ill again. Quaffed a !oFH this time and killed him along
with some more priests.
- Opened the door, went to the altar and .... it was Set's!

I couldn't believe I had finally made it. Whooyeah! I used my last wish
on a blessed figurine of a water nymph (even orcish barbarians need a
girlfriend in heaven), offered the amulet and was bathed in radiance...



